; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Pet Phone Book
; CATEGORY: Lists & Data Structures
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     association list, lookup, lists, readlist, interactive
; SUMMARY:  Keeps pet names and their owners in an association list, a list of little pairs, and lets you look them up.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   An association list is a list whose members are pairs, like
;   [[Rex Sam] [Tiger Mia]]. The first item of each pair is the key
;   and the second is the value. The program prints the book, looks
;   up pets you type, and adds new pets you tell it about.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Type a pet name in the command center and press Enter. If the
;   pet is new, you are asked for its owner. Type quit to finish.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * lists of lists as a tiny database
;   * FIND with a template to search for a key
;   * FPUT to add a new pair at the front
;   * FILTER to delete a pair
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Store three things per pet: name, owner and kind of animal.
;   * Add a "forget" command that uses FORGET to remove a pet.
;   * Print the book sorted by owner.
; ============================================================

make "book [[Rex Sam] [Tiger Mia] [Bubbles Leo] [Nibbles Ava]]

; FIND runs the template on each pair and outputs the first pair for
; which it says true. If nothing matches, FIND outputs the empty list.
to lookup :pet
  output find [equalp first ? :pet] :book
end

to remember :pet :owner
  make "book fput (list :pet :owner) :book
end

; FILTER keeps every pair whose key is NOT the pet, so the pair vanishes.
to forget :pet
  make "book filter [not equalp first ? :pet] :book
end

to showbook
  print [--- The pet phone book ---]
  foreach :book [print (sentence first ? [belongs to] last ?)]
  print []
end

to ask.owner :pet
  print sentence [Who owns] word :pet "?
  localmake "answer readlist
  if emptyp :answer [stop]
  remember :pet first :answer
  print (sentence [Saved.] :pet [belongs to] first :answer)
end

to chat
  forever [
    print [Type a pet name, or quit:]
    localmake "line readlist
    if emptyp :line [stop]
    localmake "pet first :line
    if equalp :pet "quit [showbook stop]
    localmake "pair lookup :pet
    ifelse emptyp :pair [
      print (sentence [I do not know] :pet [yet.])
      ask.owner :pet
    ] [
      print (sentence :pet [belongs to] last :pair)
    ]
  ]
end

showbook
forget "Nibbles
print [Nibbles moved away, so the book now has:]
showbook
chat
